<%#
Cistergraphia: the scriptorium (fol. 2v)
========================================

Purpose:
- The reader's game. A game plate brought to Read opens as its puzzle: the
  reading desk for an intact one, the bench to restore a worn one, the board
  to rejoin a broken one. The decoder's answer stays one click away, below

Design Decisions:
- The page is built from the file alone, never from the message: which signs
  are worn, what their strokes allow, where the fragments' edges are. The
  scribe's plate page knows more; this one cannot, and says so
- The same bench, board and plate figure as the plate page (partials), so the
  two pages play the same
- "Decipher it" posts the same file back with decipher=1: the solver, for a
  reader who wants the answer, or has one to check
- A plate won (read to the end, every pair balanced, whole again) is counted
  in the scriptorium record, by rung (data-play), kept in the browser; the
  reserved line says so

Constraints:
- Worn plates under a grille play once the key is given; broken plates
  follow the snail. Sealed plates are not games
- A ruined plate is the board first, then (rejoined=1, from the board once
  whole) the bench on the plate drawn whole from its own fragments; the file
  carried on to the decoder is still the broken one
%>
<% rung = if @broken || @rejoined then @weathered ? 'ruined' : 'broken'
          elsif @desk then 'intact'
          else 'worn'
          end %>
<section class="leaf" aria-labelledby="play-title" data-play="<%= rung %>">
  <p class="folio-mark" aria-hidden="true">fol. 2<sup>v</sup></p>
  <h1 id="play-title" class="rubric"><%= if @broken then @weathered ? 'A plate to rejoin and restore' : 'A plate to rejoin'
                                            elsif @desk then 'A plate to read'
                                            else 'A plate to restore'
                                            end %></h1>
  <% if @rejoined %>
    <p class="lede">Whole again: the fragments are rejoined, and the plate has lost <%= @entries.size %> <%= @entries.size == 1 ? 'stroke position' : 'stroke positions' %>, hatched where the surface is worn. Now restore it: press the lost digits back in, each pair of signs must sum to a value on the tablet, and where two or three letters balance, the words decide.</p>
  <% elsif @desk %>
    <p class="lede">The plate is whole: <%= @values.size / 2 %> pairs of signs, each summing to a letter on the tablet. Read it pair by pair: type what each sign reads and the page adds them. Guided, a tap on a sign shows its value; unaided, a wrong reading is marked, never corrected, and three in a row earn the Lectio’s ranks.</p>
  <% elsif @broken && @weathered %>
    <p class="lede">The plate came in <%= fragments_count(@fragments.size) %>, worn where the surface is hatched. Lay them on the board, turned where need be: a join holds when every pair of signs can balance, whatever its lacunae held. Whole again, it reads as an edition, and the bench opens on it to restore what is lost.</p>
  <% elsif @broken %>
    <p class="lede">The plate came in <%= fragments_count(@fragments.size) %>. Lay them on the board, turned where need be: only one arrangement makes every pair of signs balance, and the shapes alone will not tell you which.</p>
  <% else %>
    <p class="lede">The plate has lost <%= @entries.size %> <%= @entries.size == 1 ? 'stroke position' : 'stroke positions' %>, hatched where the surface is worn. Press the lost digits back in: each pair of signs must sum to a value on the tablet. Where two or three letters balance, the words decide.</p>
  <% end %>

  <dl class="specs">
    <div><dt>Signs</dt><dd><%= @size * @size %></dd></div>
    <div><dt>Grid</dt><dd><%= @size %> × <%= @size %></dd></div>
    <div><dt>Layout</dt><dd><%= @broken ? 'Phaistos' : layout_name(@layout) %></dd></div>
    <% if @broken %>
      <div><dt>Condition</dt><dd><%= @weathered ? "Ruined: #{fragments_count(@fragments.size)}, worn" : "Broken, in #{fragments_count(@fragments.size)}" %></dd></div>
    <% elsif @rejoined %>
      <div><dt>Condition</dt><dd>Ruined, rejoined: worn</dd></div>
    <% elsif @desk %>
      <div><dt>Condition</dt><dd>Intact</dd></div>
    <% else %>
      <div><dt>Condition</dt><dd><%= @tally ? 'Worn, with tally signs' : 'Worn' %></dd></div>
    <% end %>
    <% if grille? %>
      <div><dt>Grille key</dt><dd><code class="grille-key"><%= @layout %></code></dd></div>
    <% end %>
  </dl>

  <% if @broken %>
    <%== erb :_board, layout: false, locals: { svg: @svg_content, fragments: @fragments, size: @size, worn: @weathered } %>
  <% elsif @desk %>
    <%== erb :_plate, layout: false, locals: { svg: @svg_content, cells: plate_cells_json(@values, @layout), geometry: plate_layout_json(@values, @layout), layout: @layout, decoy: nil } %>
    <%== erb :_desk, layout: false, locals: { values: @values, tablet: Cistergraphia::CHARACTERS } %>
  <% else %>
    <%== erb :_plate, layout: false, locals: { svg: @plate_svg || @svg_content, cells: plate_cells_json(@values, @layout, @damage), geometry: plate_layout_json(@values, @layout), layout: @layout, decoy: nil } %>
    <%== erb :_bench, layout: false, locals: { entries: @entries, values: @values, damage: @damage, tally: @tally } %>
  <% end %>

  <p class="record" data-record="play" aria-live="polite"></p>

  <form class="readback" method="post" action="/decode">
    <h2 class="index-heading">Ask the decoder</h2>
    <input type="hidden" name="svg" value="<%= @svg_content %>">
    <input type="hidden" name="decipher" value="1">
    <% if grille? %><input type="hidden" name="grille" value="<%= @layout %>"><% end %>
    <div class="readback-row">
      <button type="submit" class="btn">Decipher it</button>
      <% if @layout == :rongorongo %>
        <button type="button" class="btn awaits-script" data-action="turn-plate" aria-pressed="false">Turn the plate</button>
      <% end %>
      <a class="btn btn--quiet" href="/decode">Read another</a>
    </div>
  </form>
</section>
